<title>JAPAN: Japan Oct domestic vehicle sales up 8.4 yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Oct domestic vehicle sales up 8.4 yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's domestic vehicle sales rose 8.4 percent from a year earlier to 447,278 units in October, the Japan Automobile Dealers Association said on Friday.</p>
<p>The October sales breakdown was as follows (with percentage changes from a year earlier):</p>
<p> Total cars		321,875  up   14.1 percent</p>
<p> - Cars over 2000 cc    88,321  up   16.0 percent</p>
<p> - Cars under 2000 cc  233,554  up   13.3 percent</p>
<p> Trucks		    124,297  down  4.0 percent</p>
<p> - Heavy trucks	    9,760  down 10.4 percent</p>
<p> - Light trucks	  114,537  down  3.5 percent</p>
<p> Buses			 1,106  up    8.1 percent</p>
<p>October sales included 33,550 imported vehicles, up 11.6 percent from the year before.</p>
<p>October vehicle sales by five major Japanese makers were as follows (with percentage changes from a year earlier):</p>
<p> Toyota Motor     195,499  up    9.7 percent</p>
<p> Nissan Motor	74,658  down  9.7 percent</p>
<p> Honda Motor	 50,258  up   46.8 percent</p>
<p> Mitsubishi Motors 36,845  up   23.2 percent</p>
<p> Mazda Motor	 24,369  down  1.0 percent</p>
